# Canonical author identities (AQU-1583).
#
# `git` applies this file to `log`, `blame`, `shortlog` and friends, so history
# attributes correctly WITHOUT rewriting it. Each line is
#   <Canonical Name> <canonical@email> <Commit Name> <commit@email>
# and maps the trailing (as-committed) identity onto the leading one.
#
# Only identities with direct evidence are merged here. If you appear twice,
# add yourself — and fix the `user.name` / `user.email` on the machine that
# produced the wrong one, because this file corrects the record, not the cause.

# `t <t@t>` is a machine with an unconfigured git identity, not a person: every
# commit authored that way reaches `dev` through a `ryder/*` branch (PRs #1835,
# #1841, #1844, #1693, #1694, #1712, #1682, #1738, and the
# `ryder/release-deploy-*` merges). Nothing in this repository sets that
# identity — the CI workflows commit as `aquilla-release-bot`, and the only
# in-tree `user.name=t` is inside throwaway temp repos in
# `scripts/release-cut.test.ts`, `scripts/tag-release.test.ts` and
# `scripts/migrate-daemon/__tests__/fetch.test.ts` — so the fix belongs in that
# machine's local/global git config.
Ryder Wishart <ryderwishart@gmail.com> t <t@t>
Ryder Wishart <ryderwishart@gmail.com> ryderwishart <ryderwishart@gmail.com>

